        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1179">

                <pb facs="0866" n="790" xml:id="pg790"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/4130</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Governor of Arizona to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Executive Office</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Phoenix</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 3, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your letter of the 28th ult., requesting the cooperation of the proper officials
                    in preventing the smuggling of arms and ammunition from Arizona into Mexico.</p>
                <p>You may be assured that I will immediately communicate with the proper officers
                    of those Arizona counties contiguous to the international boundary, urging them
                    to adopt all measures necessary to prevent illicit traffic in firearms and
                    ammunition.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. W. P. Hunt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
